    "result_text": "All 256 tests pass, including both new acceptance tests. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when no registration date is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and `registrationDate` is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (input) and `OwnerDto` (output) both gain the field, and MapStruct maps it automatically by name. `format: date` generates a `java.time.LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD` \u2014 matching the spec.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, default `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the client didn't supply one, before saving. A supplied date is preserved.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. This is required because the test profile (`hsqldb`) runs with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema comes entirely from `schema.sql`. Applied to all four dialects for consistency.\n\nResult: the two new acceptance tests (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) pass, and the full suite is green \u2014 **256 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.",
